{{also|lineup|line-up}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/laɪn.ˈʌp/|nocount=1}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-lineup.ogg|Audio (CA)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|engineering}} to put in [[alignment]]; to put in correct adjustment for smooth running<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|line}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put things in a [[line]]
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To get into a [[line]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1962|month=April|author=J. N. Faulkner|title=Summer Saturday at Waterloo|journal=Modern Railways|page=263|text=For the steam services, passengers with reserved seats are assembled behind the appropriate notice boards in the centre cab road, which is barred to motor traffic on summer Saturdays. Unreserved passengers '''line up''' behind other boards, which merely display destinations and not departure times.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|sports}} To [[start]] a game in a certain position on the playing field.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=February 6, 2011
|author=Alistair Magowan
|title=West Ham 0 - 1 Birmingham
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9385585.stm
|page=
|passage=The Nigerian forward '''lined up''' on the left of a front three with Keane in the middle and Frederic Piquionne on the right, and it was from Keane's lay-off that the former Portsmouth striker curled a shot straight at Ben Foster on 20 minutes.}}
# To make arrangements for an event.
#: ''A number of famous actors and musicians have been '''lined up''' for the celebrations.''
# To [[support]] a group or movement.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=April 23, 2012
|author=Angelique Chrisafis
|title=François Hollande on top but far right scores record result in French election
|work=the Guardian
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2012/apr/23/francois-hollande-french-election
|page=
|passage=The final vote between Hollande and Sarkozy now depends on a delicate balance of how France's total of rightwing and leftwing voters '''line up'''.}}
# To [[agree]] or [[correspond]].
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=December 1, 2017
|author=Tom Breihan
|title=Mad Max: Fury Road might already be the best action movie ever made
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=https://www.avclub.com/mad-max-fury-road-might-already-be-the-best-action-mov-1820691831
|page=
|passage=Fury Road is a long way away from being a political tract, but it is a story about heroic women overcoming the influence of a predatory, proprietary, evil man, and I do think that matters. In any case, I’ve been doing my best to enjoy politically repellant action movies for my entire life, and I can’t even tell you how great it is that my favorite action movie of all time happens to have ideas about life that '''line up''' with my own. That’s one of Fury Road’s many miracles.}}

